<p>The first two operations involve adding and removing key-value pairs. Sp=
ecifically, we need the ability to remove a key-value pair from one end of =
a data structure (representing the least recently used end) and add a key-v=
alue pair to the other.</p>
<p>Which data structure allows us to efficiently add or remove an element f=
rom it? A suitable data structure for these operations is a linked list, pa=
rticularly because we can add and remove a node in constant time if we have=
 a reference to that node. But should we use a singly or doubly linked list=
?</p>
